    026 Phase 1b Task 1: GPU/broadcast path for euler_exp
    
    - _euler_exp forks on storage type like _euler: Array keeps the scalar
      exp(dt*L) loop (now _euler_exp_cpu!), device stores take
      _euler_exp_broadcast!, which evaluates the frozen-gradient action
      q = exp(dt*L)*Gamma matrix-free by substepped order-8 Taylor matvecs
      (substep count from the field-wide max of a dt*|L| bound; fits the
      existing 11 scratch rows, no per-particle 3x3 exponential).
    - Scalar path's non-finite-ratio DomainError guard enforced post-hoc via
      one masked reduction; substep budget guards corrupted fields.
    - CoreSpreading euler_exp blended diffusion gets the missing isa-Array
      fork plus _corespreading_eulerexp_broadcast! (expm1 blend from M[9]).
    - Device paths skip dsigma2_* splitting accumulators (existing precedent).
    - New parity testset (loop vs broadcast, both stretching conventions,
      mild + multi-substep regimes, dt=0, DomainError edges, CoreSpreading
      twin) in runtests_gpu_fmm.jl; 020 Phase-2R expint suite stays 28/28.
    
